,"/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle of the county&rsquo;s grids July to August and August to September each came in under 90% of normal in 39 of 75 years. In 2025, June to July came in at 9% of normal on the middle, and May to June at 44%. So far in 2026, May to June and June to July each sit at 50% of normal on the middle. Grid 26172 had its driest year in 1966, at 57% of normal.</p>"}
